## Run locally

1. Install Python 3.10 or newer.
2. Get a free Gemini API key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
3. In a terminal:

```bash
# create and activate a virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

pip install -r requirements.txt

# provide your key (or paste it into the sidebar when the app opens)
export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"     # Windows PowerShell: $env:GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"

streamlit run app.py
```

The app opens at http://localhost:8501.

## Configuration

| Setting | How to set it | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | environment variable or Streamlit secret | asked in the sidebar if missing |
| `GEMINI_MODEL` | environment variable or Streamlit secret | `gemini-2.5-flash` |

The model name can also be changed in the sidebar. If Google retires or renames a model, change this value; no code edit is needed.

## Push to GitHub (using the website, no command line)

1. Sign in at https://github.com and click **+** (top right) → **New repository**.
2. Name it, for example `ats-resume-checker`. Choose **Public** (needed for the free Streamlit Community Cloud plan unless you connect a private repo), tick **Add a README file** is optional, then click **Create repository**.
3. In the repository, click **Add file** → **Upload files**.
4. Drag in `app.py`, `requirements.txt` and `README.md`. If a README already exists, GitHub will ask to replace it; that is fine.
5. Scroll down, type a commit message such as `Add ATS resume checker`, keep **Commit directly to the main branch**, and click **Commit changes**.

> Never upload your API key. Keep it only in Streamlit's Secrets (below) or in your own environment.

## Deploy on Streamlit Community Cloud

1. Go to https://share.streamlit.io and sign in with GitHub. Allow access to your repositories when asked.
2. Click **Create app** → **Deploy a public app from GitHub**.
3. Choose your repository, branch `main`, and set **Main file path** to `app.py`.
4. Click **Advanced settings**. In **Secrets**, paste:

   ```toml
   GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key-here"
   ```

   Optionally pick a Python version (3.11 or 3.12 works well).
5. Click **Deploy**. The first build takes a few minutes while it installs `requirements.txt`.
6. You get a public URL like `https://your-app-name.streamlit.app`.

To change the key later: open the app → **Manage app** → **Settings** → **Secrets**. Any push to `main` redeploys the app automatically.

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| "Gemini rejected the request" | The API key is wrong or the model name is invalid. Check both. |
| "model name was not found" | Set a current Flash model in the sidebar or `GEMINI_MODEL`. |
| "rate limit reached" | You hit the free-tier limit. Wait a minute and retry. |
| "Almost no text could be extracted" | The PDF is a scanned image. Export a text-based PDF or DOCX. ATS software cannot read images either. |
| "password protected" | Upload an unlocked copy. |
| Build fails on Streamlit Cloud | Make sure `requirements.txt` is in the repo root, not a subfolder. |

## Privacy

The resume text and job description are sent to the Gemini API for analysis. The app does not save uploaded files or results to disk; results live only in your browser session. If you deploy a public instance, tell your users that their text is processed by Google's API, and consider whether that suits the data you handle.

